/** \fn IMPORT_C TBool CFont::GetCharacterPosition2(TPositionParam &aParam, RShapeInfo &aShapeInfo) const
Takes Unicode text and produces the glyph cluster for the first character in that text plus any combining mark characters, or for the first indic syllable. It is responsible for contextual glyph selection, ligature creation and diacritic placement.

CFont::TPositionParam

\param aParam The input/output parameter of the text/glyph data for the algorithm.

\param aShapeInfo The function will cache &quot;shaped&quot; text (e.g. complex scripts such as Devanagari) here. aShapeInfo must be freshly-constructed or closed for each new piece of text in aParam.iText. If aParam.iText is unchanged between calls, aShapeInfo should be passed back in unchanged as well.


